      "question_1": "What fraction of B_AME does each exact order capture?",
      "answer_1": "The FULL closed form captures only 19.6% (D) → 3.1% (⁴He) of B_AME on the Q_β scale (the 10A−5 residual), so every order is bounded by that ceiling. The expansion is ALTERNATING with g_i ≈ 0.5–0.7 (not small): order-1 overshoots B_pred, order-2 corrects down, order-3 up — the many-body 'hierarchy' of the interface product is NOT perturbative.",
